<title>CANADA: Russel Q4 shr turns to loss after charge.</title>
<headline>Russel Q4 shr turns to loss after charge.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			    1995</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$2.35     loss	C$0.10</p>
<p> Net	   loss     118,541     loss	 3,685</p>
<p> Revs		     346,190		  322,046</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$2.42   profit	C$0.10</p>
<p> Net	   loss     118,468   profit	 9,730</p>
<p> Revs		   1,447,715		1,491,675</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full name is Russel Metals Inc. Fourth-quarter 1996 results included a pre-tax provision of C$50 million to cover potential future costs and losses related to disposition of non-core assets and discontinued operations. In the same period Russel also elected to reverse Canadian deferred taxes recoverable previously recorded on the balance sheet aggregating about C$69 million.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
